===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|en|fruit}}
{{dercat|en|qsb-grc}}
From {{inh|en|enm|date}}, from {{der|en|fro|date|id=fruit}}, {{m|fro|datil}}, {{m|fro|datille}}, from {{der|en|la|dactylus}} (likely via {{der|en|oc-pro-old|datil}}), from {{der|en|grc|δάκτυλος|t=finger}} (from the resemblance of the date to a human finger), probably a folk-etymological alteration of a word from a {{der|en|sem}} source such as {{der|en|ar|دَقَل|t=variety of date palm}} or {{der|en|he|דֶּקֶל|tr=deqel|t=date palm}}. {{dbt|en|dactyl|dactylus}}. Displaced native {{noncog|ang|fingeræppel}}, literally "''[[finger]]-[[apple]]''".

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q1652093}}The [[fruit]] of the [[date palm]], {{taxfmt|Phoenix dactylifera|species}}, somewhat in the shape of an [[olive]], containing a soft, sweet pulp and enclosing a hard kernel. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|We made a nice cake from '''dates'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|Q25292}}The [[date palm]]. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|There were a few '''dates''' planted around the house.}}
# {{lb|en|AU|NZ}} The [[anus]]. {{defdate|from 20th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1996|author={{w|Peter Doyle}}|title=Get Rich Quick
|passage=The bullet took the middle finger of his right hand clean off {{...}}. ‘He sure won't be sticking ''that'' finger up his '''date''' again,’ said Max.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author={{w|Melissa Lucashenko}}|title=Too Much Lip|publisher=University of Queensland Press|year_published=2023|page=88
|passage=Black Superman could kiss his '''date''', the little faggot.}}

